{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "obs-demo-session-11",
    "name": "FoodFast Observability Demo",
    "description": "Session 11 — Observability & Monitoring\n\nRuns 17 requests across 4 phases to produce meaningful time-series data in Aspire Dashboard and Grafana Cloud.\n\n## How to run in Postman\n1. Open Collection Runner (▶ button)\n2. Select environment: FoodFast Local\n3. Set **Delay** to **3000 ms** between requests\n4. Click **Run FoodFast Observability Demo**\n\nFor a richer histogram (more data points), set **Iterations** to 2 or 3.\n\n## What to watch in Aspire Dashboard (http://localhost:18888)\n- **Structured Logs** — filter by Level to see Warning and Error events stand out\n- **Metrics** — watch foodfast.payment.duration_ms spike during Phase 2 and 3\n- **Traces** — compare the 5-span happy path waterfall vs the truncated error traces\n\n## Loyalty tiers in this collection\n- new_user_* → Bronze (0 prior orders in DB)\n- Alice, Bob, Charlie, Eve → Silver (5 seeded orders each)\n- Gold tier (10+ orders) appears on 2nd/3rd iteration run",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Phase 1 — Baseline",
      "description": "Establish healthy baseline traffic. All requests succeed. Metrics climb steadily.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health Check",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"API is healthy — status 200\", () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"Returns array of orders\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "orders"]
            },
            "description": "Verify the API is up before running scenarios."
          }
        },
